title: 'txpool: hold the transaction pool as a trait object instead of a wrapper'

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |-
      `TransactionPoolWrapper` existed only to give the boxed transaction pool a sized type that
      could travel through the generic `Arc<Pool>` parameters used across the service builder. The
      pool is now referenced directly as `Arc<dyn FullClientTransactionPool<Block, Client>>`, which
      `TransactionPoolHandle` aliases, so the extra layer of forwarding is gone.

      `BuildNetworkParams`, `BuildNetworkAdvancedParams`, `SpawnTasksParams` and
      `GenRpcModuleParams` no longer carry a transaction pool type parameter, and the client bound
      they need is spelled out once as the new `sc_transaction_pool::ClientForTransactionPool` trait.
      Components that keep the pool behind an `Arc` (the RPC servers, the proposer factory, manual
      seal, mixnet) accept unsized pools now, which is a relaxation and needs no changes on their
      side.

      `ClientForTransactionPool` pins the `BlockIdTo` error to `sp_blockchain::Error`, which every call
      site already required, so the long client bound lists on `build_network`, `spawn_tasks`,
      `gen_rpc_module` and the transaction pool `Builder` collapse to that single trait plus the few
      capabilities each one genuinely adds.

      Migration for nodes outside this repository

      - `sc_transaction_pool::Builder::build` hands back an `Arc` already, so drop the surrounding
        `Arc::from(..)` at the construction site.
      - Drop the transaction pool type argument where `BuildNetworkParams`,
        `BuildNetworkAdvancedParams`, `SpawnTasksParams` or `GenRpcModuleParams` are named
        explicitly, since the client and block types now determine it.
      - Add `?Sized` to any generic parameter that holds the pool behind an `Arc`, because
        `TransactionPoolHandle` is a trait object and no longer has a statically known size.
      - A hand written client type has to use `sp_blockchain::Error` as its `BlockIdTo` error to
        satisfy `ClientForTransactionPool`.

